Ownership:
 "Type : User, Group, Other"
 w = write
 x = execute
 r = read

Options: Change the behavior of a file(aftrer ls command)
  - -l = display file permissions
  - -a = display hidden files
  - -la = combination of -l and -a

chmod : change permission of a file and directory
- example command : chmod g+x,o-r note.txt
	- g+x = grant permission for group to execute file
	- o-r = disallow permission for other to read file
	- note : dont put space after comma
chown : change ownership of a file or directory

